extraction_notes: |
  - Dragons and Gods printed 40-42 (cache p041-p043, page_offset 1); the stat block starts at the foot of printed 40 and runs to the Rifts conversion on printed 42, where the Thunder Lizard begins. Printed 41 and 42 were rendered and every number read off the render; the text layer''s digit cipher (206 for 2D6, l0 for 10) disagreed with it throughout.
  - PLAYER CHARACTER: printed 50, Hatchling Dragon as an optional Player Character, allows a hatchling of most species (not the Hydra, Cockatrice or Wooly Dragon), with the shared dragon experience table and no starting possessions (starting_money 0, equipment_starting empty). Imported 2026-09-27 on Nate''s decision, in the shape of chiang-ku-dragon: a hatchling and an adult variant, the hatchling first.
  - XP: the Dragon Exp. Table, printed 17, read off a render. The book prints 30 levels; the fifteen lower bounds stored are levels 1-15 (0 to 600,001). Levels 16-30 run 800,001 / 1,000,001 / 1,250,001 / 1,500,001 / 2,000,001 / 2,500,001 / 3,000,001 / 3,500,001 / 4,000,001 / 5,000,001 / 6,000,001 / 7,000,001 / 10,000,001 / 20,000,001 / 40,000,001.
  - POOLS AND DICE are per variant, as printed. The hatchling S.D.C. prints as 3D6x100 plus 2D6 per level (the text layer garbles it; the render reads 3D6x100). A.R. is prose, as on the Chiang-Ku.
  - ATTACKS: attacks_base per variant, four for the hatchling and six for the adult; no Hand to Hand style is printed or granted.
  - SAVES: "+1 on all other saving throws" (hatchling; +3 adult) is stored on each of the sheet''s d20 saves other than horror factor, which is stated separately. Coma/death is a percentile roll and is left alone.
  - MAGIC AND PSIONICS are the HATCHLING''s, because a variant cannot override either block and the hatchling is the player character. The adult''s are the two special abilities above. The hatchling line says all warlock magic from levels one and two; it is read as the AIR warlock spells (judgement), because the adult''s own magic is all air elemental spells and an adult knowing less than its hatchling would make no sense. The 20 Air: warlock rows at levels 1-2 are granted by name; the 1D4 more from levels 3-4 at each later level is dice-valued, which a spells_schedule count cannot hold, so it is prose in the Magic Knowledge ability (the cats-eye hatchling precedent, and the convention of the other hatchlings imported the same day).
  - PSIONICS: five sensitive and five physical as starting groups, two more (either category) at levels 4, 8 and 12.
  - SKILLS: the R.C.C. list at the adult''s percentages, as the book prints it. The hatchling rule (languages and basic math at 98%, everything else at first-level proficiency) needs no override here: every other skill is a catalog base plus a printed bonus, which is its first-level proficiency. Scholar is the catalog''s Technical, as on the Chiang-Ku. Literacy in two other languages plus four more spoken is six Language: Other picks and two Literacy: Other picks, the literate two counted among the six (judgement). The picks are written as bonuses on the catalog rows (Language: Other 50 +48, Literacy: Other 30 +68, 98% at first level), because regression refuses a language pick frozen with a base. Climb 90/80% and swim 90% are natural abilities, granted as Climbing and Swimming at fixed figures (the Hawrk precedent). Track by smell 45% has no catalog row and is prose.
  - The Rifts conversion (M.D.C. 1D4x1000+100 adult, 1D4x100+20 hatchling; two Rifts skills from Communications, Pilot, Science, Technical and modern W.P.) is a different system''s stats and is not stored.
  - Alignment (any, typically anarchist 30% or evil: 30% miscreant, 25% diabolic, 5% aberrant), size, weight, habitat, life span, enemies and allies are in the body.
